            <div xml:id="d753">

                <pb facs="0716" n="708" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg708"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/7181</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Adviser on
                        Political Relations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hornbeck</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-12-07">December 7, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In the course of a conversation this morning, Lord Lothian informed me in
                    confidence that the British Government has informed the Chinese Ambassador in
                    London that the British Government will advance £5,000,000 for further support
                    of Chinese currency and will make for China a credit of £5,000,000 for the
                    making of purchases within the sterling area. The British Foreign Office has
                    inquired of the Ambassador whether he would consider December 10 an opportune
                    moment for making public announcement of this decision. The Ambassador remarked
                    to me that it seemed to him “the sooner the better,” and he asked my opinion. I
                    replied that I perceived no objection to the date December 10 or any time
                    between now and then.</p>
                <closer><signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">tanley</hi>] K. H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ornbeck</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
